{"study_accession":"PRJEB32800","secondary_study_accession":"ERP115521","title":"DNA Hydroxymethylation is Associated with Disease Severity and Persists at Enhancers of Oncogenic Regions in Multiple Myeloma","description":"Multiple myeloma (MM) is a heterogeneous plasma cell malignancy that remains challenging to cure. Global hypomethylation correlates with an aggressive phenotype of the disease while hypermethylation is observed at particular regions of myeloma such as B cell-specific enhancers. The recently discovered active epigenetic mark 5-hydroxymethylCytosine (5hmC) may also play a role in tumor biology, however, little is known about its level and distribution in myeloma. In this study, we investigated the global level and the genomic localization of 5hmC in myeloma cells from 40 newly diagnosed patients, including paired relapses, and of control individuals.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":8,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMEA5670916","study_accession":"PRJEB32800","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"Plasma Cells from the Bone Marrow","description":"Plasma Cells from the Bone Marrow","sex":"","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2019-10-29","attributes":[["ENA-CHECKLIST","ERC000011"],["ENA-FIRST-PUBLIC","2019-10-29T17:04:13Z"],["organism","Homo sapiens"],["ENA-LAST-UPDATE","2019-05-31T10:40:14Z"],["scientific_name","Homo sapiens"],["common name","human"],["cell_type","plasma cell"],["tissue_type","bone marrow"],["ENA-FIRST-PUBLIC","2019-10-29"],["ENA-LAST-UPDATE","2019-05-31"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"ERR3347670","experiment_accession":"ERX3372244","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"Oligo-dT","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":24368569,"base_count":1218428450,"first_public":"2019-10-29","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMEA5670917","study_accession":"PRJEB32800","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"